# Git Workflow Rules

## Core Rule

**Never** commit directly to `main`. Every change is developed on a branch and merged into main via a PR.

## Branch Naming

```
<type>/<linear-id>-<short-description>

feat/dra-14-category-crud
feat/dra-15-thread-listing
fix/dra-22-mention-notification-bug
chore/dra-8-coolify-deploy-setup
refactor/dra-16-post-pagination
```

| Prefix | Usage |
|--------|-------|
| `feat/` | New feature |
| `fix/` | Bug fix |
| `chore/` | Configuration, tooling, dependency updates |
| `refactor/` | Code improvement without behavior change |
| `docs/` | Documentation-only change |

## Commit Message Format (Conventional Commits)

**All commit messages must be in English.**

```
<type>(<scope>): <description>

feat(threads): add pagination to thread list
fix(auth): redirect to login when session expires
chore(deps): update prisma to 6.x
refactor(queries): extract thread queries to separate file
```

### Type List

| Type | When |
|------|------|
| `feat` | New feature |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `chore` | Build, config, dependencies |
| `refactor` | Restructuring |
| `style` | Format/style only (no behavior change) |
| `test` | Adding/editing tests |
| `docs` | Documentation |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |

### Scope Examples

`auth`, `threads`, `posts`, `categories`, `users`, `admin`, `db`, `ui`, `api`

## Working with Multiple Agents (Claude Code + Cursor)

To avoid conflicts when two agents work simultaneously:

- **Each agent works on a different branch** — never work on the same branch concurrently
- Check branch status with `git status` before starting a new task
- Before committing, stay up to date with `git pull origin main --rebase`
- If two agents are editing the same file simultaneously → finish one, merge it, then start the other

## PR Rules

- PR title in commit format: `feat(threads): add pagination`
- Include Linear issue ID in PR description: `Closes DRA-15`
- Before merging to main:
  - [ ] Build passes (`npm run build`)
  - [ ] No TypeScript errors (`tsc --noEmit`)
  - [ ] Tests pass if any exist

## Forbidden Actions

- Direct push to `main` branch
- `git push --force` (to main)
- `.env` file in a commit
- Commit containing `console.log` (remove development logs before committing)
- Commit containing `TODO:` comments (open a Linear issue instead)
